From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 09:30:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add cfm_agent_v_3_4: v3.3 architecture plus v2.2 scenario
 and calibration work

Merges the two CFM lines. v3.3's numerical architecture, graduated evidence
tiers, sanitizer, ensemble-locked control, and Python-owned arithmetic are
preserved unchanged. Three ideas come across from the v2.2 event-scoring line.

Pillar boundary: the evidence skill now bans structured market data and
supply/demand statistics or agency publications as claims, using a general
boundary test rather than a list of named series. This keeps the LLM pillar
from restating what the quant and physical pillars already see.

Driver categories: every claim carries a driver_category (geopolitical,
weather, operational, policy, demand_expectations), orthogonal to claim_type.
claim_type says what kind of fact a claim is; driver_category says what kind
of driver produced it.

Competing scenarios: 2-3 categorical scenarios with probabilities summing to
1, a direction, a magnitude, and one required low-probability, high-impact
tail case. Scenarios state no prices, matching the categorical-action design.
Malformed sets are rejected; an absent set is tolerated and degrades to v3.3
behaviour. The policy then applies a scenario-derived uncertainty floor: a
two-sided scenario set forces the interval wider whatever the LLM proposed.
The floor widens only and never moves the center, so it is deliberately
independent of the evidence tier and cannot manufacture a directional view.

Calibration feature row: prediction metadata now carries a fixed-width numeric
row built from the sanitized assessment. Every key exists on every run, which
is what makes it usable as regression input when claim text varies between
origins. With the unadjusted_ensemble already recorded, this supplies both
sides of the study that would replace v3.3's hand-set policy constants with
fitted values.

Validation in the repo environment: ruff clean, compileall clean, 33 tests
passing (17 inherited from v3.3 unchanged, 16 new). Also fixed the 9 ruff
errors v3.3 shipped with.

cfm_agent_v_2_0, v_2_1, v_2_2, and v_3_3 are unmodified.
