From e8f8402137738bdb14f2c5dbd90d73878dc2b178 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 09:30:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Close fundamentals leak and duplicate scenarios in v2.2
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rebuilds the four fixes applied and live-tested during the session.

Skill scope: the exclusion list becomes two banned classes (structured
market data; supply/demand statistics and agency publications) plus a
general boundary test — a factor must be an event or a situation, never
a statistic another pillar will see in its own input data.

Search strategy: step 1 targets events rather than "market drivers" or
"market outlook" queries, which return supply/demand-framed market-wrap
articles. New step 4 allows overview articles to point at an event but
never to serve as its evidence.

Search instruction: replaces the short generic version with the richer
one adapted from the analyst agent — let results decide what matters,
name both sides of a disagreement, seek a historical precedent, and
verify recency from substance rather than claimed publish dates. Scope
line covers the five event categories, and the events-not-statistics
rule is repeated at the retrieval layer where wrap articles enter.

Duplicate scenarios: a new validator rejects two scenarios identical in
both stances and impact_score. Shared stances alone stay legal, so an
intensity ladder (de-escalation / sustained / escalation) still passes
while a tail case that merely restates the mainline does not.

Verified in the repo environment: ruff clean, 20 tests passing.
